{"name":"Pink Heath","hex":"#f2bddf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"heath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tract of level uncultivated land with sandy soil and scrubby vegetation; heathland.","Any small evergreen shrub of the family Ericaceae.\n\nin Erica spp.\nin Cassiope spp.\nin Daboecia spp.\nin Epacris spp. (Australian heath)\nin Leucopogon spp. (beard heath)\nin Phyllodoce spp. (mountain heath)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Epacris impressa","blocks":[{"text":"Epacris impressa, also known as common heath, is a species of plant in the heath family Ericaceae. It is native to south-eastern Australia. French botanist Jacques Labillardière collected the species in 1793 and described it in 1805. Four forms have been identified, but no subspecies are recognised. Growing in heathland, shrubland or open forest, it is generally a small shrub around 0.5 to 1 m tall, with small stiff leaves. The red, pink or white tube-like flowers appear from late autumn to early spring. Honeyeater birds, particularly the eastern spinebill, feed upon the nectar of the flowers. It regenerates after bushfire by seed or by resprouting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Epacris_impressa_Pink_Form.jpg/330px-Epacris_impressa_Pink_Form.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epacris_impressa","wikidata":"Q2494794"},{"title":"Heath","blocks":[{"text":"A heath is a shrubland habitat found mainly on free-draining infertile, acidic soils and is characterised by open, low-growing woody vegetation. Moorland is generally related to high-ground heaths with—especially in Great Britain—a cooler and damper climate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Amrum_%28187753235%29.jpeg/330px-Amrum_%28187753235%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heath","wikidata":"Q27590"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Epacris_impressa_pink_6942.jpg/500px-Epacris_impressa_pink_6942.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Epacris_impressa_pink_6942.jpg/1280px-Epacris_impressa_pink_6942.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Epacris_impressa_pink_6942.jpg/500px-Epacris_impressa_pink_6942.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Erect habit, Belgrave South, Victoria","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEpacris_impressa_pink_6942.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Epacris_impressa_white_3984.jpg/500px-Epacris_impressa_white_3984.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Epacris_impressa_white_3984.jpg/1280px-Epacris_impressa_white_3984.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Epacris_impressa_white_3984.jpg/500px-Epacris_impressa_white_3984.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEpacris_impressa_white_3984.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Common_Heath.jpg/500px-Common_Heath.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Common_Heath.jpg/1280px-Common_Heath.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Common_Heath.jpg/500px-Common_Heath.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACommon_Heath.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Epacris_impressa_red_5755.jpg/500px-Epacris_impressa_red_5755.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Epacris_impressa_red_5755.jpg/500px-Epacris_impressa_red_5755.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEpacris_impressa_red_5755.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Acanthorhynchus_tenuirostris_female.jpg/500px-Acanthorhynchus_tenuirostris_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Acanthorhynchus_tenuirostris_female.jpg/1280px-Acanthorhynchus_tenuirostris_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or